    "global": {
      "kind": "dossier optimality/uniqueness proof",
      "statement": "With both coefficients free, a finite MLE exists exactly for nonconstant samples. Its locations are all sample medians, and its scale is unique. The location is unique exactly when the median interval is a singleton. With location held, a unique positive scale MLE exists unless every observation equals that location, when the likelihood is unbounded. With positive scale held, all sample medians maximize the likelihood, including the unique common value for constant samples. Holding both coefficients leaves likelihood evaluation.",
      "reason": "Let $A(\\mu)=\\sum_i|x_i-\\mu|$. This convex function is minimized precisely on the median interval and is constant there. For $A>0$, maximizing $-n\\log b-A/b$ gives the unique scale $b=A/n$. The profiled likelihood decreases strictly in $A$, so all and only medians maximize it. If $A=0$, the likelihood grows without bound as $b\\to0$."
